.TH NEOGENERA 1 "2026" "NeoGenera 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neogenera \- a Lisp environment in the spirit of the Symbolics Genera workstations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neogenera
[\fB\-i\fR \fIIMAGE\fR] [\fB\-\-ui\fR] [\fB\-\-load\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-eval\fR \fIFORM\fR] [\fB\-\-save\-image\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-toplevel\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NeoGenera is a Common Lisp subset with a bytecode compiler written in itself, a text-mode window system with
mouse-sensitive output, an Emacs-style editor, developer tools (Inspector, cross-reference, trace, stepper,
profiler), an integrated hypertext documentation system, and libraries for mathematics, statistics and
bioinformatics.
.PP
Without options it starts a line-mode Listener with the interactive debugger. With
.B \-\-ui
it starts the window system, which needs a terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " IMAGE"
Start from the heap image IMAGE (default: the world image installed with the program).
.TP
.B \-\-ui
Run the window system.
.TP
.BI \-\-load " FILE"
Load FILE before the Listener starts. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-eval " FORM"
Evaluate FORM before the Listener starts. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-image " FILE"
Save the heap as an image after the loads and evaluations (written atomically).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-toplevel
Exit after processing the options instead of starting a Listener.
.TP
.B \-\-gc\-stress
Collect garbage at every safe point (testing).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NG_IMAGE
Image to use when \-i is not given.
.TP
.B NG_SOURCE_ROOT
Directory holding the lisp/ and docs/ trees, used by the editor and documentation viewer to find source files.
Set by the neogenera wrapper script.
.TP
.B NEOGENERA_HOME
Directory for the settings file (default ~/.neogenera).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <prefix>/lib/neogenera/neogenera.img
The world image. It is tied to the binary beside it and checked with a checksum when loaded.
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/doc/neogenera/html
The manuals and API reference (also available inside the system with :doc).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
neogenera --ui
neogenera --no-toplevel --eval '(print (expt 2 100))'
neogenera --no-toplevel --load analysis.lisp
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Images and Lisp files are programs: only load ones you trust. See docs/SECURITY.md in the source tree.
.SH SEE ALSO
Inside the system: :help, :doc, :tutorial.
